{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.realisation_volume_compatibility","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.realisation_volume_compatibility","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/RealisationVolumeCompatibility.lean#L81-L90","doc":"**Conditional consequence (motivic content), derived from the class — name-compat with the old\n`lean.ref`.** Given the coincidence `compat`, the two realizations agree: `τ_∞ β = R_top β`. The\narchimedean and the topological/motivic realizations of the one volume motive produce the same\nvalue. This is fully verified **modulo the class instance**; the class instance for the framework's\nactual realizations is the open conjecture (not proved here). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:archimedean-realisation-volume-compatibility","label":"conj:archimedean-realisation-volume-compatibility","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/archimedean-realisation-volume-compatibility.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.compat_is_restrictive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.compat_is_restrictive","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/RealisationVolumeCompatibility.lean#L71-L79","doc":"**The `compat` field is a genuine restriction (§3b-tax non-degeneracy).** Not every triple of\nmaps satisfies the coincidence: constants `τ_∞ = 0`, `V_hyp = 1` violate it. So the class asserts\nreal content — it is not auto-satisfiable for arbitrary realizations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.instRealisationVolumeCompatibilityReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.instRealisationVolumeCompatibilityReal","kind":"instance","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/RealisationVolumeCompatibility.lean#L61-L69","doc":"**The class is non-vacuous (shape-witness).** Taking all three realizations to be the identity\non `ℝ` gives a triple satisfying `compat` — the structural shape is inhabited. This witnesses the\nshape is realizable; it does **not** assert that the framework's genuine `τ_∞` / `R_top` coincide\n(there is no instance for the actual realization functors). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.compat","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/RealisationVolumeCompatibility.lean#L59-L59","doc":"**Content — the motivic coincidence.** Both realizations agree with the hyperbolic volume on\nevery braid: `τ_∞ β = V_hyp β` *and* `R_top β = V_hyp β`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.Vhyp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.Vhyp","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/RealisationVolumeCompatibility.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.Rtop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.Rtop","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/RealisationVolumeCompatibility.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Topological / motivic realization `R_top` of the volume class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.tauInfty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.tauInfty","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/RealisationVolumeCompatibility.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Local archimedean realization `τ_∞`: the Habiro-ring `q₀`-evaluation of the volume class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/RealisationVolumeCompatibility.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.RealisationVolumeCompatibility.RealisationVolumeCompatibility","kind":"class","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/RealisationVolumeCompatibility.lean#L44-L59","doc":"**conj:archimedean-realisation-volume-compatibility (§3b class).** A QOU volume datum on a type\nof braids carries **two distinct realizations** — the local archimedean realization `tauInfty` (the\nHabiro-ring `q₀`-evaluation `τ_∞`) and the topological / motivic realization `Rtop` — together with\nthe hyperbolic volume `Vhyp`. The content (`compat`) is the **motivic coincidence**: both\nrealizations agree with `Vhyp` on every braid. That the framework's *actual* `τ_∞` and `R_top`\nrealize one motive this way is the open conjecture; the class only names the shape. ","signatureChunk":0}]}